  <ferc:CompanyIdentifier id="f-19" contextRef="c-1">C004254</ferc:CompanyIdentifier>
  <ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock id="f-20" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;1. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:10.8pt;text-indent:-10.8pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;2. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="padding-left:10.8pt;text-indent:-10.8pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;3. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;4. See Note 6 - &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-style:italic;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Legal and Environmental Matters&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt; in the Notes to the Financials Statements on Page 122 for additional detail.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;5. None&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:StatementAboutImportantChangesDuringTheQuarterYearTextBlock>
  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-21" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;1.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Description of Business &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Tallgrass Pony Express Pipeline, LLC ("Pony Express") is a Delaware limited liability company that provides crude oil transportation to customers in Wyoming, Colorado, Kansas, and the surrounding regions, with access to Bakken Shale, DJ Basin and Powder River Basin production. Pony Express owns an approximately 1,050-mile crude oil pipeline with origins in Wyoming, Colorado, and Kansas and destinations in Colorado, Kansas and Oklahoma.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The sole member of Pony Express as of June 30, 2026 was Liberty Express Pipeline, LLC ("LEP"). The member interests and voting rights in LEP as of June 30, 2026 are as follows:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:14.5pt"&gt;75% of the outstanding units - Tallgrass LEP Holdings, LLC ("Tallgrass LEP Holdings"), an indirect subsidiary of Tallgrass Energy Partners, LP ("TEP"); and&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;padding-left:36pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;&#8226;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%;padding-left:14.5pt"&gt;25% of the outstanding units - Bridger Pipeline LLC ("Bridger").&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Prior to January 1, 2026, Tallgrass LEP Holdings held a 100% preferred membership interest in LEP. On January 1, 2026, Tallgrass LEP Holdings sold twenty-five percent (25%) of the outstanding preferred units in LEP to Bridger. Immediately following the consummation of such sale, each outstanding preferred unit in LEP automatically converted into one common unit in LEP. As a result, Tallgrass LEP Holdings and Bridger now own 75% and 25% of the membership interests in LEP, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;padding-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The accompanying unaudited interim financial statements were prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission ("FERC") as set forth in its applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which is a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America. In management's opinion, these interim financial statements reflect normal and recurring adjustments that are necessary for a fair statement of Pony Express&#8217; financial results for the interim periods presented, and adequate disclosures have been made to make the information presented not misleading. These interim financial statements should be read along with Pony Express&#8217; financial statements and related notes included in its 2025 Annual Report of Oil Pipeline Companies on Form No. 6.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;padding-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;3.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;Related Party Transactions &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Pony Express has no employees. LEP has an operating agreement with Tallgrass LEP Operator, LLC ("Tallgrass LEP Operator"), an indirect subsidiary of TEP, under which Tallgrass LEP Operator provides and bills LEP and its subsidiaries an annual operating fee and for various services at cost, including certain employee labor costs, field expenses, and insurance for property and casualty risks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Totals of transactions with affiliated companies are as follows (in thousands):&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="margin-bottom:6pt;margin-top:6pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:96.428%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:22.511%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:19.424%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;t